<!-- 01 — THE SITUATION -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — The situation</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Two decisions, one after the other</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">In the listing meeting, the buyer asks about margin, rate of sale, gaps in the range and risk. What matters is whether the product uses the shelf metre better than what stands there today. A beautiful pack design answers none of these questions.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Once the product is listed, someone else decides: the shopper at the shelf, within seconds, usually without reading. For many retailer brands and for brands without an advertising budget, the pack is the only sales tool.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">So the packaging has to convince twice: once at the meeting table, once on the shelf.</p>
</section>

<!-- 02 — WHAT IS CREATED -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">02 — What is created</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">For the buyer and for the shopper</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    {%- for item in [
      "Packaging as a system: a constant brand header for recognition, an order that makes the range accessible without reading, fixed positions for the information shoppers look for",
      "Sell-in material for the listing meeting: range logic, placement on the shelf, arguments on margin and rate of sale",
      "A sales test before production starts, using proprietary procedures — the results double as arguments in the listing meeting",
      "Labelling for several countries when the range goes into export"
    ] %}
    <li class="check-item reveal reveal-delay-{{ loop.index0 % 3 }}">
      <span class="check-icon"></span>
      <span>{{ item }}</span>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<!-- 03 — TRADEMARK LAW -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">03 — No risk on the shelf</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Trademark law belongs in the design, not in a check afterwards</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A retailer brand is often meant to move deliberately close to a manufacturer brand. If the pack is perceived as an imitation, a cease-and-desist letter looms — and even an unjustified one can strain a listing or a supply relationship.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The likelihood of confusion is therefore checked while the design is being developed. Knowing the limit before the design is fixed saves rounds of corrections and makes full use of the latitude up to that point.</p>
</section>

